diff:1747660899:1747659315:=266,268c266,267%0a%3c %25red%25TO BECOME OBSOLETE%25%25, replaced by [[#msg.branch.flags| $msg.branch.flags]]%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a---%0a> %0a> %0a272,273c271%0a%3c '''$branch''' - this variable is used for creating new branches by writing into it the value of a SIP URI.\\%0a%3c %25red%25TO BECOME OBSOLETE%25%25, replaced by [[#msg.branch.uri| $msg.branch.uri]]%0a---%0a> '''$branch''' - this variable is used for creating new branches by writing into it the value of a SIP URI.%0a295d292%0a%3c %25red%25TO BECOME OBSOLETE%25%25, replaced by [[#msg.branch.uri| $msg.branch.uri]]\\%0a322,324c319,320%0a%3c '''$branch.flag(flag_name)[]''' - this variable provides read/write access to the value of a single certain branch flag (identified by name). The values accepted for writing are 1 (set) and 0 (unset). The returned values are 1/"true" (set) and 0/"false" (unset). An index is accepted, in order to access the flag for a certain branch. By default the 0 (or current) branch accessed (for more on index, see the the [[#branch.fields|branch.fields]] variable) - note that "*" is not accepted.\\%0a%3c %25red%25TO BECOME OBSOLETE%25%25, replaced by [[#msg.branch.flag| $msg.branch.flag]]%0a%3c %0a---%0a> '''$branch.flag(flag_name)[]''' - this variable provides read/write access to the value of a single certain branch flag (identified by name). The values accepted for writing are 1 (set) and 0 (unset). The returned values are 1/"true" (set) and 0/"false" (unset). An index is accepted, in order to access the flag for a certain branch. By default the 0 (or current) branch accessed (for more on index, see the the [[#branch.fields|branch.fields]] variable) - note that "*" is not accepted.%0a> %0a603,661d598%0a%3c @]%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c [[#msg.branch.duri]]%0a%3c !!!! Destiation URI of a message branch - $msg.branch.duri [[#msg.branch.duri|&#x1F517;]]%0a%3c %0a%3c '''$msg.branch.duri''' -  100%25 similar to [[#msg.branch.uri| $msg.branch.uri]], but operating with the Detination-URI value of the message branch.%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c [[#msg.branch.path]]%0a%3c !!!! PATH of a message branch - $msg.branch.path [[#msg.branch.path|&#x1F517;]]%0a%3c %0a%3c '''$msg.branch.path''' -  100%25 similar to [[#msg.branch.uri| $msg.branch.uri]], but operating with the PATH value of the message branch.%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c [[#msg.branch.q]]%0a%3c !!!! Q of a message branch - $msg.branch.q [[#msg.branch.q|&#x1F517;]]%0a%3c %0a%3c '''$msg.branch.q''' -  100%25 similar to [[#msg.branch.uri| $msg.branch.uri]], but operating with the Q value of the message branch.%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c [[#msg.branch.flags]]%0a%3c !!!! Flags of a message branch - $msg.branch.flags [[#msg.branch.flags|&#x1F517;]]%0a%3c %0a%3c '''$msg.branch.flags''' -  100%25 similar to [[#msg.branch.uri| $msg.branch.uri]], but operating with list (comma separated) of per-branch flags (which are set for the branch).%0a%3c %0a%3c [[#msg.branch.socket]]%0a%3c !!!! SIP socket of a message branch - $msg.branch.socket [[#msg.branch.socket|&#x1F517;]]%0a%3c %0a%3c '''$msg.branch.socket''' -  100%25 similar to [[#msg.branch.uri| $msg.branch.uri]], but operating with the (forced) socket value of the message branch.%0a%3c %0a%3c [[#msg.branch.flag()]]%0a%3c !!!! A flag of a message branch - $msg.branch.flag() [[#msg.branch.flag|&#x1F517;]]%0a%3c %0a%3c '''$msg.branch.flag()''' -  similar to [[#msg.branch.uri| $msg.branch.uri]], but operating over a single branch flag (for the current branch).\\%0a%3c The accepted values are 0 for FALSE, pozitive non-zero for TRUE. The returned values are 0 for FALSE and 1 for TRUE.\\%0a%3c NOTE: the '''*'''/ALL index cannot be used here.%0a%3c [@%0a%3c    # creates a new branch%0a%3c    $msg.branch = "sip:new@domain.org";%0a%3c    # set the "pstn" named flag for this branch%0a%3c    $msg.branch.flag(pstn) = 1;%0a%3c    $msg.branch.flag(foo) = 1;%0a%3c    # print all the set flags%0a%3c    xlog("Flags are %3c$msg.branch.flags>\n");%0a%3c @]%0a%3c %0a%3c [[#msg.branch.attr()]]%0a%3c !!!! An attribute of a message branch - $msg.branch.attr() [[#msg.branch.attr|&#x1F517;]]%0a%3c %0a%3c '''$msg.branch.attr()''' -  similar to [[#msg.branch.uri| $msg.branch.uri]], but operating over a single branch attribute (attached to the current branch).\\%0a%3c An attribute can have whatever name (no need to be pre-defined) and it can have a single value (at a time), string or integer.\\%0a%3c NOTE: the '''*'''/ALL index cannot be used here.%0a%3c [@%0a%3c    # creates a new branch%0a%3c    $msg.branch = "sip:new@domain.org";%0a%3c    # set the "pstn" named flag for this branch%0a%3c    $msg.branch.attr(name) = "one";%0a%3c    $msg.branch.attr(num) = 5;%0a
