diff:1747659315:1747310477:=572,599d571%0a%3c %0a%3c [[#msg.branch]]%0a%3c !!!! Message branch - $msg.branch [[#msg.branch|&#x1F517;]]%0a%3c %0a%3c '''$msg.branch''' - similar to [[#branch|$branch]], this variable is used for creating new message branches by writing into it the value of a SIP URI. By reading this variable, you get the SIP URI of the current/last added branch (or of the RURI branch if no additional branch was added so far).%0a%3c [@%0a%3c    # creates a new branch%0a%3c    $msg.branch = "sip:new@domain.org";%0a%3c    # print its URI%0a%3c    xlog("last added branch has URI $msg.branch \n");%0a%3c @]%0a%3c %0a%3c %0a%3c [[#msg.branch.uri]]%0a%3c !!!! SIP URI of a message branch - $msg.branch.uri [[#msg.branch.uri|&#x1F517;]]%0a%3c %0a%3c '''$msg.branch.uri''' -  gives read / write access over the SIP URI (as string) of an existing message branch. The message branches are created via [[Documentation.Script-CoreFunctions-4-1#append_branch|append_msg_branch()]] core function or by various modules (like "registrar" module). The message branches are consumed by the TM "t_relay()" function (they are converted to TM branches).\\%0a%3c The variable supports indexing - it starts from 0, meaning the RURI (or message) branch. The newly added branches will start from 1. So the branch 0 exists all%0a%3c the time, there is no need to creat it. If no index is specified, the current/last added branch (or of the RURI branch if no additional branch was added so far) will be considered. Negative values are also accepted, meaning indexing from the last branch ( -1 is the latest/higher branch) to the RURI branch. An '''*''' / ALL index will return the comma separated list with the values from all branches.\\%0a%3c The variable can be used in REQUEST and FAILURE routes.%0a%3c [@%0a%3c    # creates a new branch%0a%3c    $msg.branch = "sip:new@domain.org";%0a%3c    # change its URI%0a%3c    $msg.branch.uri = "sip:new_new@domain.org"%0a%3c    # change its URI of RURI branch%0a%3c    $(msg.branch.uri[0]) = "sip:new_RURI@domain.org"%0a%3c @]%0a
